<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dharmapala (Pala emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th–9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dharmapala was the second ruler of the Pala Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, reigning from about 770 to 810. He extended Pala power up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, installing his protégé <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakrayudha">Chakrayudha</a> as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, and fought the Gurjara-Pratiharas and the Rashtrakutas for northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. A Buddhist patron, he founded the monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramashila">Vikramashila</a> and Somapura at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somapura-mahavihara">Paharpur</a>.</p></div>
